@* A tab's editing controls, shown to every role and editable only by those who may: for anyone
   else the area is a disabled fieldset, so the browser disables every input, select and button
   in it, the systm components' included, while the values stay readable. The actions outside it
   (New, Import, Save) are left out by the tab itself, and its save methods refuse on their own
   too. A Viewer reads a dataset's boost rules, synonyms, query parameters and Search or ask
   settings this way (Nov 2026; before, those tabs were hidden from viewers, though the API let
   them read every one). *@
<fieldset class="indx-readonly-area" disabled="@(!Editable)">
    @ChildContent
</fieldset>

@code {
    [Parameter] public bool Editable { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
